    <statement><p>Determine the truth value of the following statements if the universe of
discourse is the set of real numbers.</p>
<p><ol>
<li>
<p><m>\exists x (x^2+2 &gt; 1)</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\forall x  (x^2 \neq x )</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\exists x (x^2= -1)</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\exists x  (x^2 &gt; x)</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\exists x \forall y (xy=0)</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\exists x (x^2=2)</m></p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</statement>
